cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this result, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Bilinear Maps in Fewer AND Gates than Rank: A Polynomial Gap Between Multiplicative and Quadratic-Circuit Complexity over F2"
abstract: >-
  For n = 4^N, every bilinear map F2^n x F2^n -> F2^n is computed by a fixed
  AND-depth-two frame with 2 n^{log_4 12} = O(n^1.7925) AND gates; only the
  XOR wiring depends on the map. By counting, almost every such map has
  bilinear rank at least n^2/3 and hence needs at least n^2/6 AND gates in
  any quadratic (level-one) circuit. So the ratio between quadratic-circuit
  and unrestricted multiplicative complexity is at least n^0.2075/12 for
  almost all bilinear maps (non-explicit). Research note; not peer-reviewed.
authors:
